 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Given M 1x1 tiles and N 2x2 tiles, return the largest side s such that an s x s square can be tiled exactly (no overlap, no gaps) using at most M small and at most N large tiles; 0 if no square can be formed. An s x s square holds at most floor(s/2)^2 large tiles, so s works iff s*s - 4*min(N, floor(s/2)^2) <= M.",
